I go near the ticket counter.
A short time ago, there was heavy rain outside.
But here in the building, it is very quiet.
A clerk sits at the counter.
I say to him, "Sir, please give one ticket."
He says, "Fifty rupees."
I give the rupees to him.
That clerk gives me that ticket.
He gives the receipt too.
I ask him, "Sir, is the upstairs exhibition open right now?"
He says, "Yes, madam, that exhibition is open."
"This path goes to the main hall."
"That staircase goes upstairs."
He points in the direction of the main hall.
I say thank you to him, and place the ticket in the bag.
Five months ago, I was afraid of the noise of this city.
But now, I like this peace.
I slowly walk inside.
